    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d273">

                <pb facs="0317" n="247" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg247"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/2757</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Barclay</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1317</seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum</hi>
                </p>
                <p>His Britannic Majesty’s Chargé d’Affaires presents his compliments to the
                    Secretary of State and, with reference to the memorandum from His Majesty’s
                    Embassy No. 1305 of November 20th, has the honour to inform him by direction of
                    His Majesty’s Government that King Hussein has asked His
                    Majesty’s Commissioner at Cairo to convey to His Majesty’s Government the formal
                    ratification of the fact that his son, Emir Feisal, is proceeding as his
                    representative to Paris. The King has also asked that a
                    similar notification may be made by the British Government in his name to the
                    United States, French, and Italian Governments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-22">November 22,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
